// Source: Pine Script v5 built-in `ta.atr()` — TradingView
// Reference: https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-reference/v5/#fun_ta{dot}atr
//
// Definition (Wilder, 1978):
//   TR   = max(high - low, |high - close[1]|, |low - close[1]|)
//   ATR  = RMA(TR, length)   where RMA = Wilder's smoothing
//   RMA(x, n) : first value = SMA(x, n) ; then rma[t] = (rma[t-1]*(n-1) + x[t]) / n
//
// Pine snippet:
//   //@version=5
//   indicator("ATR")
//   length = input.int(14, "Length")
//   atr = ta.atr(length)
//   plot(atr)
